1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,300
August again, my son.
The Dambi Doolloo rain still

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:05,350
taps this roof,
the way it did when

3
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:06,350
you were small.

4
00:00:08,233 --> 00:00:10,978
Eebbisaa, your guitar still
leans by the wall.

5
00:00:10,978 --> 00:00:13,478
You would sit there
humming over your tea,

6
00:00:13,478 --> 00:00:15,673
making fighting songs
on six strings.

7
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:18,808
You weren't just a singer.
You taught neighborhood

8
00:00:18,808 --> 00:00:20,375
kids Qubee—
our Oromo alphabet—

9
00:00:20,375 --> 00:00:22,620
so they could finally spell
their own names.

10
00:00:23,236 --> 00:00:26,142
People listened to your
cassettes in secret.

11
00:00:26,142 --> 00:00:29,386
I still keep your old tape
and notebook of lyrics

12
00:00:29,386 --> 00:00:30,670
folded in my shawl.

13
00:00:31,244 --> 00:00:33,557
Your blue ink still
fills this notebook.

14
00:00:33,557 --> 00:00:35,218
Before leaving for
Finfinnee,

15
00:00:35,218 --> 00:00:37,659
the capital, you sang to me:
'Mother of a hero,

16
00:00:37,659 --> 00:00:38,659
do not cry.'

17
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:41,668
In August 1996,
a bullet in Finfinnee

18
00:00:41,668 --> 00:00:44,220
took your voice.
Ever since that night,

19
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:46,570
this house has been
empty and quiet.

20
00:00:47,248 --> 00:00:49,761
For years I couldn't bear
to touch it.

21
00:00:49,761 --> 00:00:52,887
Tonight, the quiet
is too heavy. I'm no singer,

22
00:00:52,887 --> 00:00:54,653
my son—let me
try one note.

23
00:00:55,250 --> 00:00:58,696
Just one old string...
They killed the singer,

24
00:00:58,696 --> 00:01:00,610
Eebbisaa. Never the song.

25
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:04,104
Listen, my son.
Outside my door,

26
00:01:04,104 --> 00:01:07,094
children who weren't even
born back then still know

27
00:01:07,094 --> 00:01:08,290
every line you sang.

28
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:12,924
Hear them? Through the
Dambi Doolloo rain,

29
00:01:12,924 --> 00:01:15,858
they are singing your
songs right back to you.

30
00:01:15,858 --> 00:01:18,010
Tonight, my son...
I will not cry.
